In article <T36273C.89Aug2225521@saha.hut.fi> t36273c@saha.hut.fi (Ari Huttunen) writes:
>
>Doors.. The *only* thing I would like to be changed is that you *can't* see
>beforehand if the door is open or closed! This can be serious if you are
>running away from a monster. Then you bump into one and loose a turn!

IMHO this is an EXCELLENT idea!  Any ideas how (i.e. what symbols to use)?
/ and \ come to mind but these already mean something.  Then again + also
means something different when not used in conjunction with a wall.  Ari
suggested > and < and these may also be usable.

      ---/---  closed?  ---\--- opened?  ---+--- no door?

or how about

     ---#---  no door or an open door and ---+--- a closed door?

or how about

     ---#--- no door   ---~--- open door and  ---+--- closed door?

